<section class="sl-section" id="services">
  <div class="sl-header">
    <div class="sl-inner">
      <div class="section-tag reveal">
        <div class="line"></div>
        <span>What We Deliver</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="section-headline reveal">Our Services</h2>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SERVICE 1 — dark navy -->
  <div class="svc-block dark" id="engineering">
    <div class="sl-inner svc-inner">
      <div class="svc-num-col">
        <div class="svc-num">01</div>
        <svg class="svc-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 014 4v14a3 3 0 00-3-3H2z"/><path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 00-4 4v14a3 3 0 013-3h7z"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-body">
        <div class="svc-label">Service 01</div>
        <div class="svc-name">Engineering &amp;<br><span class="accent">Design Services</span></div>
        <p class="svc-desc">Every Jayveecons project begins with engineering. Before fabrication starts, our team evaluates process requirements, material characteristics, site conditions, operational goals, and maintenance considerations to develop equipment engineered specifically for each application — not adapted from standard catalogue designs.</p>
        <p class="svc-desc">At the core of this capability is the <span class="accent">Jayveecons Vectrix™ Design Platform</span> — a unified engineering environment built around decades of accumulated process knowledge, calculation methodologies, field experience, and equipment performance data across multiple industries.</p>
        <div class="svc-points">
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Process Engineering:</strong><br>Capacity calculations, material flow analysis, process optimization, equipment selection, and sizing based on bulk density, particle size distribution, moisture, temperature, and throughput requirements.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Machine Design:</strong><br>Shaft and bearing calculations, structural analysis, drive selection, power sizing, conveyor geometry, elevator configurations, and heavy-duty component integration.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Detailed Fabrication Engineering:</strong><br>General arrangement drawings, manufacturing drawings, weld detailing, assembly documentation, and bill of materials.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Civil &amp; Layout Integration:</strong><br>Foundation load data, anchor bolt layouts, equipment positioning, plant layout coordination, and interface support.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Material &amp; Application Engineering:</strong><br>Grade selection for abrasion, corrosion, high-temperature service, food-grade compliance, and specific operating environments.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Reverse Engineering &amp; Upgrades:</strong><br>Documentation, redesign, and performance improvement of existing equipment including modernization and wear optimization.</div></div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact?service=engineering" class="svc-cta">Discuss your engineering requirements <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SERVICE 2 — light -->
  <div class="svc-block light" id="fabrication">
    <div class="sl-inner svc-inner">
      <div class="svc-num-col">
        <div class="svc-num">02</div>
        <svg class="svc-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 000 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 001.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 01-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 01-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 017.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-body">
        <div class="svc-label">Service 02</div>
        <div class="svc-name">In-House<br><span class="accent">Manufacturing</span></div>
        <p class="svc-desc">Jayveecons Group along with our partner AkshayVipra El-Mec, manufactures a wide range of bulk material handling, thermal processing, storage, and process equipment for demanding industrial applications. Our 90,000 sq.ft integrated manufacturing facility in Bengaluru combines fabrication, machining, assembly, and quality control within a single operation.</p>
        <div class="svc-points">
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Plate Rolling &amp; Forming:</strong><br>Rolling and forming of conveyor troughs, kiln shells, silos, hoppers, tanks, ducts, and large-diameter cylindrical structures.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Heavy Structural Fabrication:</strong><br>Fabrication of conveyor galleries, support structures, platforms, frames, chutes, and industrial steel assemblies. MIG, TIG, and arc welding across carbon steel, stainless, and AR alloys.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Precision Machining:</strong><br>CNC machining and precision turning of shafts, pulleys, flanges, bearing housings, idler assemblies, couplings, and custom components.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Materials:</strong><br>Mild steel, AR steels, stainless 304/316, high-temperature materials, and food-grade specifications.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Quality Control &amp; Assurance:</strong><br>Dimensional verification, weld inspection, pressure testing, trial assembly, and pre-dispatch quality inspections.</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Assembly &amp; Factory Acceptance Testing:</strong><br>Precision assembly with comprehensive factory performance testing to ensure site readiness and operational reliability.</div></div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact?service=fabrication" class="svc-cta">Discuss fabrication requirements <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SERVICE 3 — dark navy -->
  <div class="svc-block dark" id="erection">
    <div class="sl-inner svc-inner">
      <div class="svc-num-col">
        <div class="svc-num">03</div>
        <svg class="svc-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><rect x="2" y="3" width="20" height="14" rx="2"/><path d="M8 21h8M12 17v4"/><polyline points="7 8 12 13 17 8"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-body">
        <div class="svc-label">Service 03</div>
        <div class="svc-name">Erection &amp;<br>Commissioning</div>
        <p class="svc-desc">Equipment that leaves our workshop performing to specification must arrive at your site performing to specification. Jayveecons' erection and commissioning teams carry the same engineering knowledge as our design team — because they are the same team. On-site, we handle mechanical assembly, shaft alignment, drive installation, electrical interlocking coordination, no-load trials, and process load commissioning.</p>
        <div class="svc-points">
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Civil coordination:</strong> survey, setting-out, and anchor bolt checking before equipment arrival</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Mechanical assembly:</strong> full equipment erection, shaft alignment, bearing setting, belt tensioning, and coupling installation</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Drive installation:</strong> gearbox mounting, V-belt or coupling alignment, VFD integration, and motor rotation checks</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>No-load trials:</strong> full-speed mechanical trial before material introduction; vibration, noise, and temperature checks</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Commissioning:</strong> material introduction, throughput ramp-up, performance measurement, and parameter optimisation</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Operator training:</strong> on-site training for your plant operators on start-up, shutdown, and routine maintenance procedures</div></div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact?service=erection" class="svc-cta">Discuss your installation project <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SERVICE 4 — light -->
  <div class="svc-block light" id="parts">
    <div class="sl-inner svc-inner">
      <div class="svc-num-col">
        <div class="svc-num">04</div>
        <svg class="svc-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M19.07 4.93a10 10 0 010 14.14M4.93 4.93a10 10 0 000 14.14M15.54 8.46a5 5 0 010 7.07M8.46 8.46a5 5 0 000 7.07"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-body">
        <div class="svc-label">Service 04</div>
        <div class="svc-name">Parts, Spares &amp;<br>Ongoing Support</div>
        <p class="svc-desc">Because we manufactured your equipment, we already have the drawings, the material specifications, and the manufacturing knowledge to produce exact replacement parts — without the reverse-engineering delay. Jayveecons maintains a spares programme for all VECTOMEC™ equipment we supply, and can manufacture replacement components for third-party equipment where our capability matches the requirement.</p>
        <div class="svc-points">
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>OEM replacement parts:</strong> exact replacements for all Jayveecons-supplied equipment, manufactured to original drawings</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Wear parts:</strong> conveyor belts, elevator buckets, screw flights, idler rollers, liner plates — high-turnover items stocked or fast-fabricated</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Third-party equipment:</strong> reverse-engineered spares for equipment from other manufacturers where we can match the specification</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Emergency supply:</strong> expedited fabrication for breakdowns affecting production — we understand the cost of downtime</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Spares register:</strong> we help clients establish and maintain a critical spares holding programme for planned shutdowns</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Upgrade components:</strong> improved-specification replacements that address known wear patterns or operational issues</div></div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact?service=parts" class="svc-cta">Order parts or discuss spares strategy <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SERVICE 5 — dark navy -->
  <div class="svc-block dark" id="repairs">
    <div class="sl-inner svc-inner">
      <div class="svc-num-col">
        <div class="svc-num">05</div>
        <svg class="svc-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M11 4H4a2 2 0 00-2 2v14a2 2 0 002 2h14a2 2 0 002-2v-7"/><path d="M18.5 2.5a2.121 2.121 0 013 3L12 15l-4 1 1-4 9.5-9.5z"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-body">
        <div class="svc-label">Service 05</div>
        <div class="svc-name">Repairs &amp;<br>Refurbishment</div>
        <p class="svc-desc">Not every problem requires new equipment. Jayveecons provides repair and refurbishment services for existing material handling and processing equipment — both our own and third-party — extending service life, restoring performance, and in many cases upgrading the original specification.</p>
        <div class="svc-points">
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Condition assessment:</strong> site visit and inspection report with repair vs replace recommendation and cost comparison</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Workshop repairs:</strong> shaft reconditioning, bearing housing repair, pulley re-lagging, belt vulcanising, structural weld repair</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>On-site repairs:</strong> field welding, emergency fixes, and planned shutdown maintenance for equipment that cannot be moved</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Refurbishment:</strong> complete strip-down, inspection, component replacement, and reassembly to like-new standard</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>Performance upgrades:</strong> capacity increases, wear-resistance improvements, and automation additions during refurbishment</div></div>
          <div class="svc-point"><div class="svc-point-bullet"></div><div class="svc-point-text"><strong>VSK refurbishment:</strong> specialist rebuilds of Vertical Shaft Kiln systems — refractory relining, grate replacement, shell repair</div></div>
        </div>
        <a href="/contact?service=repairs" class="svc-cta">Request a repair or refurbishment assessment <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</section>

